nt status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKAHISA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIDE KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI TAKAHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI TAKAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIDE, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKAHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Latex products which are nontacky and clean; and processes for producing the products. A carboxyl-blocking agent is added to a carboxylated latex or a layer treated with a carboxyl-blocking agent is formed on one or both sides of a carboxylated latex film. Thus, an emulsion/latex product which is nontacky and clean is produced. Furthermore, by adding an aluminic salt or an aluminum hydroxide gel to a latex, a latex product which is sulfur-free and has excellent durability can be produced. Also provided is a fingerstall which is powder-free and clean and has been mechanically rolled up on the machine.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des produits de latex non collants et propres ainsi que des procédés de production des produits. Un agent bloquant carboxyle est ajouté à un latex carboxylé ou un latex traité avec un agent bloquant carboxyle est formé sur une des deux faces d'un film de latex carboxylé. Ainsi, un produit d'émulsion/latex non collant et propre est produit. De plus, par addition d'un sel alumineux ou d'un gel d'hydroxyde d'aluminium à un latex, un produit de latex sans soufre et présentant une excellente durabilité peut être produit. L'invention concerne également un doigtier sans poudre et propre ayant été enroulé mécaniquement sur la machine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>